# norc-claude-worker config. Two ways to run:
#
# A) Zero-config self-registration (what the dashboard "Remote Claude Code" prompt uses).
#    Set NORC_URL + NORC_REGISTER_TOKEN; the worker generates its own secret, detects its
#    Tailscale address, and registers itself. Nothing else required.
NORC_URL=
NORC_REGISTER_TOKEN=

# B) Manual: register the agent in the dashboard yourself and set the matching secret here.
#    Only needed if you are NOT using self-registration above.
# NORC_SHARED_SECRET=

# ── Optional (sensible defaults) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Port the worker listens on (NORC dispatches + heartbeats here). Default 8080.
# PORT=8080

# Override the URL NORC reaches the worker on. Default: auto-detected Tailscale IP.
# WORKER_PUBLIC_URL=http://100.x.y.z:8080/

# Agent name in NORC. Default: claude-<hostname>.
# AGENT_NAME=claude-mybox

# The Claude Code CLI. Must be installed AND logged in (subscription). Default 'claude'.
# CLAUDE_BIN=claude

# Optional model override (else Claude Code's default for the account).
# CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-opus-4-6

# Pin every task to one repo; otherwise each task gets its own dir under WORK_DIR.
# DEFAULT_CWD=/srv/repos/my-project
# WORK_DIR=/var/lib/norc-claude-worker

# Concurrency, per-job hard timeout (ms), liveness heartbeat cadence (ms).
# MAX_CONCURRENCY=2
# JOB_TIMEOUT_MS=1800000
# HEARTBEAT_MS=90000

# Where registration credentials + the per-page session map are stored.
# CREDENTIALS_FILE=/var/lib/norc-claude-worker/credentials.json
# SESSIONS_FILE=/var/lib/norc-claude-worker/sessions.json

# Advanced: extra args appended to every `claude -p` call (space-separated).
# CLAUDE_EXTRA_ARGS=--add-dir /srv/shared
